    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for that. Could you get a bit more specific on the wear and tear aspect? Specifically, I'm worried about how these surfaces handle heavy foot traffic over a 10-year period—like scratching, scuffing, or losing their finish. Which one is most likely to look \"beaten up\" or damaged after a few years of constant use?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Polished concrete handles foot traffic exceptionally well, though very heavy abrasive scouring could dull the finish over a decade without protective coatings. Natural stone, particularly if it is a softer marble, can suffer from etching due to acidic spills, causing permanent surface dulling. LVT is highly resistant to surface scratching but prolonged, heavy abrasive scuffing could eventually wear down the top protective layer.",
      "source": "target",
